Looking at the examples above,
Example 1) has no explicit callout of dependencies, so the React compiler will provide the simplest memoized code 
Example 2) Has explicit call out of dependencies (that is, suboptimal), so the React compiler will respect those memo hints.

If you have the following hook 

``` jsx
function useHook() {
  const expensiveFunction = useGetExpensiveFunction();
  const cheapFunction = useGetCheapFunction();

  return useMemo(() => {
    const intermediate = cheapFunction();
    return expensiveFunction(intermediate);
  }, [expensiveFunction, cheapFunction]);
}
```

you get 
``` jsx
import { c as _c } from "react/compiler-runtime";
